+## `beforeSession` error propagation
+
+- `beforeSession` is inside the `try` block, so a throw there reaches the `catch`/`finally` blocks, firing both `onError` and `afterSession`, where a deployer can assume no tools were run and the turn was aborted before provider interaction ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L34)).
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
